From: NanoKVM build <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: enable gadget buffer DMA on cv18xx/sg200x

The upstream cv1800 params (63aa7ab955e7 "usb: dwc2: add support for
Sophgo CV18XX/SG200X series SoC") force both host_dma and g_dma off with
no stated rationale, leaving the gadget in interrupt-driven slave mode.

On the SG2002 (NanoKVM), slave mode breaks f_mass_storage as a boot
device for the managed host: enumeration and small bulk-IN payloads
(READ_CAPACITY, 8 bytes) work, but the first full 512-byte bulk-IN data
packet of a READ(10) is never transmitted. The host (RPi 5 EEPROM
bootloader) times out after 10s, and its recovery read then receives the
*previous* command's CSW -- the IN pipe runs one transfer behind and the
BOT state machine never recovers (both LUNs dead until bus reset):

    MSD READ_CAPACITY ... block-count 1050658 block-size 512
    MSD cmd timeout xfer-state 2 req lba 0..0
    CBW  55 53 42 43 08 00 00 00 ... 28 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 00
    CSW  55 53 42 53 07 00 00 00 ...   <- tag 7 answering tag 8
    MSD error 7

The controller advertises internal DMA (GHWCFG2 arch = 2), and buffer
DMA is what the cvitek vendor kernel always used on this core. Cache
maintenance for non-coherent DMA demonstrably works on this kernel (SD
via dw-mshc and stmmac ethernet both do DMA). Descriptor DMA stays off:
dwc2_check_params() already rejects g_dma_desc on this core.

host_dma is left off: the NanoKVM DTS pins dr_mode = "peripheral", so
the host path never runs.

Not upstream -- local to this build.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ static void dwc2_set_cv1800_params(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 	p->otg_caps.hnp_support = false;
 	p->otg_caps.srp_support = false;
 	p->host_dma = false;
-	p->g_dma = false;
+	p->g_dma = true;
 	p->speed = DWC2_SPEED_PARAM_HIGH;
 	p->phy_type = DWC2_PHY_TYPE_PARAM_UTMI;
 	p->phy_utmi_width = 16;
